+## Authentication
+
+The verified public English Tabelog sources require no account or API key. Optional MCP uses stdio and starts only when explicitly invoked.
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+# Check the command setup without network requests or writes.
+tabelog-pp-cli doctor --dry-run
+
+# Get a compact Tokyo bar shortlist in the source's highest-rated order.
+tabelog-pp-cli find --area tokyo --cuisine bar --meal dinner --budget-max 5000 --limit 5 --agent
+
+# Fetch the canonical SAMBOA BAR Ginza ten page before using its cached ID.
+tabelog-pp-cli show https://tabelog.com/en/tokyo/A1301/A130101/13005012/ --agent
+
+# Save the fetched candidate and a personal note.
+tabelog-pp-cli lists add tokyo-bars 13005012 --note "Ginza bar option" --agent
+
+# Compare the saved facts and notes without network requests.
+tabelog-pp-cli lists compare tokyo-bars --agent
+
+# Inspect missing evidence and snapshot age before further fetching.
+tabelog-pp-cli lists audit tokyo-bars --require hours,payment,reservation,dinner_budget --max-age 24h --agent
+
+```
+
 ## Unique Features
 
-| Command | Result |
-|---|---|
-| `lists add` | Fetched candidates and personal notes in named lists |
-| `lists compare` | Offline comparison of saved facts and notes |
-| `lists refresh` | Current facts, changes and visible per-ID failures |
-| `lists alternatives` | Saved backups matching explicit constraints |
-| `lists audit` | Unfetched, source-unknown and old evidence identified separately |
+These capabilities aren't available in any other tool for this API.
 
-`lists show`, `lists note`, and `lists remove` maintain notebooks. Notes survive source refreshes; failed requests preserve valid snapshots. See [saved-list semantics and examples](docs/saved-lists.md).
+### Offline decisions
+- **`lists compare`** — Compare saved restaurants, meal budgets and personal notes without network requests.
+
+  _Use this when choosing between candidates already saved for the trip._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists compare tokyo-bars --agent
+  ```
+- **`lists alternatives`** — Find saved substitutes matching a candidate's verified area, category and optional meal budget.
+
+  _Use this when choosing a backup from the saved set using specific known facts._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists alternatives tokyo-bars --for 13005012 --match area,category --meal dinner --budget-max 5000 --agent
+  ```
+
+### Freshness and evidence
+- **`lists refresh`** — Update selected saved restaurants and see changed facts while keeping personal notes.
+
+  _Use this when a saved candidate needs current facts before a meal decision._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists refresh tokyo-bars 13005012 --agent
+  ```
+- **`lists audit`** — See which saved candidates have unfetched, unknown or old facts before requesting more details.
+
+  _Use this to select the exact saved candidates that need further checking._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists audit tokyo-bars --require hours,payment,reservation,dinner_budget --max-age 24h --agent
+  ```
+
+### Trip notes
+- **`lists add`** — Keep fetched restaurants and personal notes in a named trip list that can be resumed offline.
+
+  _Use this after fetching a candidate that should remain in the trip shortlist._
+
+  ```bash
+  tabelog-pp-cli lists add tokyo-bars 13005012 --note "Ginza bar option" --agent
+  ```
 
